    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0010",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "The [`GKGraph`](gkgraph.md) class uses this method in pathfinding between nodes—the [`findPath(from:to:)`](gkgraph/findpath(from:to:).md) method finds the lowest-cost path between a specified pair of nodes.",
      "normalizedSource": "The [`GKGraph`](gkgraph.md) class uses this method in pathfinding between nodes—the [`findPath(from:to:)`](gkgraph/findpath(from:to:).md) method finds the lowest-cost path between a specified pair of nodes.",
      "sourceHash": "07ac303dd8d0b9c3499a30c62b68a3a5d1299024d6dc7b88305f124d6c02cf2d",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Discussion",
      "contextAfter": "For the [`GKGraphNode`](gkgraphnode.md) base class, the cost of travel along any connection is 1, so the [`findPath(from:to:)`](gkgraph/findpath(from:to:).md) method simply counts connections, finding the path that involves traveling through the fewest number of nodes.",
      "documentTitle": "cost(to:)",
      "framework": "GameplayKit",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0002",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0010",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "For the [`GKGraphNode`](gkgraphnode.md) base class, the cost of travel along any connection is 1, so the [`findPath(from:to:)`](gkgraph/findpath(from:to:).md) method simply counts connections, finding the path that involves traveling through the fewest number of nodes.",
      "normalizedSource": "For the [`GKGraphNode`](gkgraphnode.md) base class, the cost of travel along any connection is 1, so the [`findPath(from:to:)`](gkgraph/findpath(from:to:).md) method simply counts connections, finding the path that involves traveling through the fewest number of nodes.",
      "sourceHash": "d9cb4db021b02a54f0d00eab3f0e236ecd7f38291c65e2fd79b2c0712b65c143",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "The [`GKGraph`](gkgraph.md) class uses this method in pathfinding between nodes—the [`findPath(from:to:)`](gkgraph/findpath(from:to:).md) method finds the lowest-cost path between a specified pair of nodes.",
      "contextAfter": "Because the subclasses [`GKGraphNode2D`](gkgraphnode2d.md) and [`GKGridGraphNode`](gkgridgraphnode.md) add geometry information to each node, those classes’ implementation of this method calculates the distance between nodes in 2D space, and the [`findPath(from:to:)`](gkgraph/findpath(from:to:).md) method finds the path with the minimum total distance traveled.",
      "documentTitle": "cost(to:)",
      "framework": "GameplayKit",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0003",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0010",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "Because the subclasses [`GKGraphNode2D`](gkgraphnode2d.md) and [`GKGridGraphNode`](gkgridgraphnode.md) add geometry information to each node, those classes’ implementation of this method calculates the distance between nodes in 2D space, and the [`findPath(from:to:)`](gkgraph/findpath(from:to:).md) method finds the path with the minimum total distance traveled.",
      "normalizedSource": "Because the subclasses [`GKGraphNode2D`](gkgraphnode2d.md) and [`GKGridGraphNode`](gkgridgraphnode.md) add geometry information to each node, those classes’ implementation of this method calculates the distance between nodes in 2D space, and the [`findPath(from:to:)`](gkgraph/findpath(from:to:).md) method finds the path with the minimum total distance traveled.",
      "sourceHash": "beead703a3ef27a1817f20823e9925e7ed27d6ad827e63ebd130c2eef980a043",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "For the [`GKGraphNode`](gkgraphnode.md) base class, the cost of travel along any connection is 1, so the [`findPath(from:to:)`](gkgraph/findpath(from:to:).md) method simply counts connections, finding the path that involves traveling through the fewest number of nodes.",
